 "paras": [
  "Lightfield updates itself from every customer interaction, so its agents can run outbound, flag deals at risk, and tell you where to focus next.",
  "The companies of the future will run on a world model of their business, not a Salesforce-era database.",
  "For agents to do customer-facing work, they need to understand how your business actually works. Legacy CRMs weren’t built for that. Layer agents on top and you get low-quality work, because the underlying data lacks the",
  "Lightfield reimagines the CRM as a world model of your business. It updates itself from every call, email, meeting, and Slack thread, assembling a context graph for agents to work from.",
  "Our agents find prospects that look like your best customers and book meetings with them. They capture commitments from every conversation and handle the follow-ups, diagnose where your funnel is weak, and learn from you",
  "And your whole company works from a shared understanding of your customers.",
  "Run account research, deal qualification, meeting prep, and follow-ups for every opportunity.",
  "Marcus’s demo last week left open questions on implementation timeline and security review. This follow-up recaps next steps and proposes times so the deal keeps moving.",
  "Great speaking last week about how Vercel is thinking about GTM tooling as you scale. I pulled together the implementation notes we discussed, including how teams typically sequence security review and rollout.",
  "Would Thursday or Friday afternoon work for a 20-minute follow-up?"
 ],
